{
  "dom_id": "step-q60194",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "In Noheli's red and white rose garden, $\\frac{3}{10}$ of the roses are red. If there are a total of $90$ roses in the garden, how many white roses are there?",
  "worked_solution": "We are given that the ratio of red roses to the total number of roses is $\\frac{3}{10}.$\n\nIn this fraction, the numerator represents the number of red roses and the denominator represents the number of  total number of roses.\n\nWe can make a denominator of $90$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by $9:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\times 9}{10\\times 9}=\\frac{27}{90}\n$$\n\nTherefore, there are $27$ red roses in the garden. Hence, the number of white roses is\n\n$$\n90-27=63.\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
